 statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy"],"id":"long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.39 (Straddle words are canonical: they agree with the greedy prefix)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.39, p. 55, label lem:straddle-agrees-greedy","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $u\\subseteq\\{1,\\ldots,d\\}$ satisfy $X_u(2)\\le1/2\\le X_u(2)+R_d$. Then\n$$\nu=G\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,d\\},\n$$\nwhere $G$ is the real greedy support for $1/2$. At the first disagreement, if $u$ takes rank $k$ and the greedy rule skips it, then $X_u(2)>1/2$. In the opposite case, the greedy remainder before $k$ is at least $w_k$, whereas the remaining contribution allowed by $u$, including $R_d$, is at most $R_k<w_k$. Both cases contradict the displayed interval. Thus there is at most one such word at each depth; the lemma does not assert its existence at every depth.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.IsStraddlePrefix.half_agrees_greedy%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-straddle-agrees-greedy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.IsStraddlePrefix.half_agrees_greedy%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.IsStraddlePrefix.hal